  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Hotel brands **commonly considered globally** for projects with a branded residences component include **Marriott** brands such as **Ritz-Carlton**, **St. Regis**, **W Hotels**, and **Edition**; **Accor** brands such as **Fairmont** and **Sofitel**; **Hilton** brands such as **Waldorf Astoria** and **Conrad**; **Hyatt** brands such as **Park Hyatt**, **Andaz**, and **Grand Hyatt**; and **IHG** brands such as **InterContinental**, **Regent**, and **Six Senses**.[2][6][7][10][11][16]\n\nAt the luxury end, **Four Seasons**, **Mandarin Oriental**, **Aman**, **Rosewood**, **Anantara**, and **Kempinski** are also frequently cited as major branded-residence operators or developer choices worldwide.[3][5][10][12][17][19]\n\nA concise way to think about the market is:\n\n- **Global scale players:** Marriott, Accor, Hilton, Hyatt, IHG[6][7][10][11][16]\n- **Luxury leaders:** Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, Mandarin Oriental, Aman, Rosewood[2][3][5][10][17][19]\n- **Other commonly seen brands:** W, Edition, Fairmont, Sofitel, Waldorf Astoria, Conrad, InterContinental, Regent, Six Senses, Anantara, Kempinski[2][3][5][10][13][16]\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into a **shortlist by segment**—for example, *ultra-luxury vs luxury vs upper-upscale*—or by **region**.",
